        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la ayuda — \"help.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin adiutare was built from iuvare, \"to give strength,\" with ad-, \"toward.\" To help was to bring your strength toward somebody. Not to take over, not to fix — to stand beside and add what you have."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English took the same stem twice. Aid is the plain one. An adjutant is the officer who stands beside a commander and adds capacity."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Said alone — ayuda — it is a call. Said with por favor, it is a request."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Your first repair word that asks for a person, not a repetition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "la ayuda",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *la ayuda*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "ayuda, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *ayuda, por favor*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "disculpe — ayuda, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *disculpe — ayuda, por favor*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What did adiutare mean, literally? (To bring strength toward.) Which English word is it, worn down? (Aid.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-C303-momento",
      "sequence": 4280,
      "title": "el momento — the tilt of a balance",
      "headword": "el momento",
      "romanization": "el momento",
      "gloss": "a moment — Latin momentum, the smallest movement that tips a balance",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:06ab85853527dff2",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two from last time, before anything new is added."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it once slowly, then at speed. see pronunciation reference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el momento — \"a moment.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin momentum came from movere, \"to move,\" and it did not mean time at all. It meant the smallest movement that tips a balance — the last grain that makes one pan drop."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is a weight, not a duration. But the tipping happens in an instant, and the word slid from the movement to the instant. English kept the original sense in momentum and the borrowed sense in moment."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un momento, por favor buys you that instant — and it is the politest thing you can say when you need to think."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two repair words now: one asks for a person, one asks for time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "el momento",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *el momento*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "un momento, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *un momento, por favor*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "un momento — no entiendo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *un momento — no entiendo*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What did momentum weigh? (The last grain that tips a balance.) What do you say to buy an instant? (Un momento, por favor.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
