        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "otra vez — \"again.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Word by word it is \"another turn.\" Vez is Latin vicem, and vicem meant a turn taken in rotation — your go, coming round again."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "English holds that exact word in several places. Vice versa is \"the turn having been changed.\" A vicar stands in somebody else's turn. A vice-president takes the turn of the president."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So otra vez does not say \"repeat.\" It says another go round — a kinder thing to ask of a stranger, and it pairs with what you already have."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three ways to repair now — ask for a person, for time, or for another go."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "otra vez",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *otra vez*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "otra vez, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *otra vez, por favor*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "más despacio, otra vez, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *más despacio, otra vez, por favor*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is a vez? (A turn, coming round.) Which English phrase hides the same word? (Vice versa.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
